Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"ab540c22-67be-4b10-a33a-9cf4acd7dc1f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CochainComplexWithPairing"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CochainComplexWithPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["degrees", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["differential", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a5be3273-a81c-412a-a9af-bc5c178a7b78"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a finite-dimensional cochain complex with a graded symmetric pairing, \
given by the degrees of the basis elements, the differential on the basis and \
the values of the pairing.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"a2ebec2d-d710-4213-9e9e-45b0ff25ca9f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CochainComplexWithPairing"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CochainComplexWithPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["degrees", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["differential", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["product", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["orientation", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ab5b5102-b148-4050-9343-e4acd933edd9"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a differential graded algebra with the pairing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"x", "y"}], "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"02fc00f9-3a8b-4304-bcaf-666ce1378e4b"],
 ", given by the products of pairs of basis elements and an orientation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b5e822a5-c919-4a2c-a955-0ab3342b2bff"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"5494a304-9e41-448b-8353-586aec4cd184"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CochainComplexWithPairing"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CochainComplexWithPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["model", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "882900f9-ed90-4a3a-9c1d-020a17ac0c41"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the finite quotient of a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModel"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModel", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "528f6e54-f935-4952-b8d6-51f8c7054c89"],
 " that agrees with it up to degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1295f296-709f-40af-9ce9-ece4e68e409a"],
 " and has its Poincar\[EAcute] duality and Hodge type.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"81355ff7-0b51-4e30-9440-e120c0ce2b52"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CochainComplexWithPairing"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CochainComplexWithPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["algebra", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "562fe5d3-32ff-43b4-a740-e1d7d9de219f"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["PoincareDualityAlgebra"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/PoincareDualityAlgebra", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "51b151e1-9b67-4c48-ab25-08e765130e90"],
 " as a complex."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"2ebb2536-b8d1-4d00-91fe-3a36a7373e19"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a tagged object, read with ",
 StyleBox["complex", "TI"],
 "[",
 StyleBox["key", "TI"],
 "] and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Normal"]], "paclet:ref/Normal"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e16541d2-3420-4477-8d8a-b8aaada71605"],
 ". It has the following keys:"
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the complex is a tagged object over an \
Association with the keys \"Degrees\", \"Differential\", \"Pairing\", \
\"Degree\" and, for an algebra, \"Product\", so that a finite complex can be \
written down and decomposed without a Sullivan model, as Example 6.1 of \
arXiv:2004.07362 over the rationals is. The three-argument form takes the \
pairing values and the four-argument form takes the product and an \
orientation and derives the pairing, since those determine a dPD algebra; \
both complete each pair given in one order by graded symmetry or \
commutativity, and both validate the data with RelationsQ and give a Failure \
instead of an object that breaks an axiom, the convention SullivanModel and \
GradedPairing follow for ill-formed data. The axioms are the relations of \
Relations since R5g, five for a complex and eleven with a product, with an \
Obstruction for each; they replace the recognizer CochainComplexWithPairingQ, \
which went with no alias. The form on a model is a quotient, not the \
subcomplex of degrees up to n+1 plus the image of the differential in degree \
n+2: that subcomplex has no monomial basis in degree n+2, while the quotient \
by everything above n+2 and by the non-pivot monomials of degree n+2 is \
isomorphic to it and is a CDGA. The form on a PoincareDualityAlgebra is the \
inverse of PoincareDualityAlgebra[complex], so no second data shape for an \
algebra enters the API. Prior art: the Wolfram Language 15.0 has no cochain \
complexes or graded pairings, and the engine of the verification suites has \
none either; T17 pins the complex of the catalogue models on their Poincare \
duality and Hodge type, and the quotient of the complex against the complex \
of the quotient.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
